From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GUIWindowVideoBase: stop thumb loader before shutdown teardown

Fixes found by the S905X5/CoreELEC driver review:

- F128 xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp:142: 0016: the loader thread left running by StopAsync outlives shutdown's texture-cache teardown, and nothing joins it until DestroyWindows

See the review diary (S905X5-DRIVER-REVIEW-DIARY.md) for the defect
analysis and the forum discussion.

final judge sign-off did not run, so this patch still needs a human
read before it is proposed upstream. Not yet exercised on S905X5 hardware.

--- a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
@@ -126,6 +126,16 @@
   return CGUIMediaWindow::OnPopupMenu(iItem);
 }
 
+void CGUIWindowVideoBase::FreeResources(bool forceUnload /* = false */)
+{
+  // Join a loader left running by StopAsync() before shutdown's UnloadSkin tears down
+  // the texture cache; the destructor runs too late.
+  if (forceUnload && g_application.IsStopping() && m_thumbLoader.IsLoading())
+    m_thumbLoader.StopThread();
+
+  CGUIMediaWindow::FreeResources(forceUnload);
+}
+
 bool CGUIWindowVideoBase::OnMessage(CGUIMessage& message)
 {
   switch ( message.GetMessage() )
--- a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.h
+++ b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.h
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
   bool OnMessage(CGUIMessage& message) override;
   bool OnAction(const CAction &action) override;
   bool OnPopupMenu(int iItem) override;
+  void FreeResources(bool forceUnload = false) override;
 
   /*! \brief Gets called to process the "info" action for the given file item
    Default implementation shows a dialog containing information for the movie/episode/...
